                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0c07cc8c-6e7d-3f05-b8e8-96d513f02d3b",
                        "entry_id": "7ae63803-fba4-32bb-a119-22898958b42d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Ancienne mesure de surface d’un terrain (358 toises carrées)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ec478e21-0a94-40e0-8b20-a542036d01b3",
                                "sense_id": "0c07cc8c-6e7d-3f05-b8e8-96d513f02d3b",
                                "text": "Pendant la guerre, il s’était contraint, tant par hygiène physique et morale que par besoin, à cultiver de ses bras, sur la route d’Alaune, un « courtil » de quelques vergées."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bf220a68-9949-4461-b4e1-cd1af4da18f7",
                        "source_entry_id": "7ae63803-fba4-32bb-a119-22898958b42d",
                        "source_sense_id": "0c07cc8c-6e7d-3f05-b8e8-96d513f02d3b",
                        "target_lang_word": "rood",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rood",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2e412cad-e989-32de-b315-831cc68f52b0",
                                        "entry_id": "ef8d0638-c604-365e-888f-f911492c6c21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A crucifix, cross, especially in a church."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c87f00a-dbde-43cf-b825-33a45e004644",
                                                "sense_id": "2e412cad-e989-32de-b315-831cc68f52b0",
                                                "text": "The Citizens in their rage, imagining that euery poſt in the Churche had bin one of yᵉ Souldyers, ſhot habbe or nabbe at randon^([sic – meaning random]) uppe to the Roode lofte, and to the Chancell, leauing ſome of theyr arrowes ſticking in the Images."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b29bcf0-1560-46ed-9e13-c68cb7ed921e",
                                                "sense_id": "2e412cad-e989-32de-b315-831cc68f52b0",
                                                "text": "Have you forgot me? No, by the rood, not so."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e3e35ddb-9406-40c1-931f-f329633686c3",
                                                "sense_id": "2e412cad-e989-32de-b315-831cc68f52b0",
                                                "text": "By holy rood, a royal beard! / How say you? we have slept, my lords. / My beard has grown into my lap."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bff04f75-5897-3de4-ae87-42ecca6fc4d5",
                                        "entry_id": "ef8d0638-c604-365e-888f-f911492c6c21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A measure of land area, equal to a quarter of an acre."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2252bbcc-c5cb-4a25-bf8e-1a90e6b00e17",
                                                "sense_id": "bff04f75-5897-3de4-ae87-42ecca6fc4d5",
                                                "text": "Next a marsh, it would seem, and now mere earth / Desperate and done with; (so a fool finds mirth, / Makes a thing and then mars it, till his mood / Changes and off he goes!) within a rood— / Bog, clay and rubble, sand and stark black dearth."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5066b366-2ccd-4639-ad03-b29207f97723",
                                                "sense_id": "bff04f75-5897-3de4-ae87-42ecca6fc4d5",
                                                "text": "[…] a bumptious fool whose god was property, not property in vast estates such as a true man might worship, but in paltry roods."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32c434b2-1881-49bf-a9d9-d099e9ec882e",
                                                "sense_id": "bff04f75-5897-3de4-ae87-42ecca6fc4d5",
                                                "text": "Perhaps, however, he could ensure against being completely alone by cultivating the few roods of garden wished upon him."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "48cdca51-499b-33fc-aab6-918586160e84",
                                        "entry_id": "ef8d0638-c604-365e-888f-f911492c6c21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An area of sixty-four square yards."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c1a8a510-c9ae-3d36-86a0-e7282f981f6e",
                                        "entry_id": "ef8d0638-c604-365e-888f-f911492c6c21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A measure of five and a half yards in length."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "dialectal",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ac21af7f-b0ae-4988-bc58-dbc7476418b8",
                                                "sense_id": "c1a8a510-c9ae-3d36-86a0-e7282f981f6e",
                                                "text": "Thus Satan […] his other parts besides / Prone on the flood, extended long and large, / Lay floating many a rood […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a531786d-4fe9-3668-a1d5-63c222b6d871",
                                        "entry_id": "ef8d0638-c604-365e-888f-f911492c6c21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The human face."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "473e6911-108b-482a-9e75-1d6a3ca5ec77",
                                                "sense_id": "a531786d-4fe9-3668-a1d5-63c222b6d871",
                                                "text": "Nou goth sonne under wode,—\nMe reweth, Marie, thi faire Rode.\nNou goth sonne under tre,—"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
